.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NQSIGN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqsign ,
.Nm nqsignd ,
.Nm nqvrfy ,
.Nm nqskg ,
.Nm nqskgd ,
.Nm nqssize ,
.Nm nqsname ,
.Nm nqsfind
.Nd ML-DSA and SLH-DSA signatures
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqskg
.Fa "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqskgd
.Fa "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *seed" "size_t seedlen"
.Fa "uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqsign
.Fa "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *msg" "size_t msglen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen"
.Fa "int ph"
.Fa "uint8_t *sig" "size_t siglen" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqsignd
.Fa "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *msg" "size_t msglen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen"
.Fa "int ph"
.Fa "const uint8_t *rnd" "size_t rndlen"
.Fa "uint8_t *sig" "size_t siglen" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqvrfy
.Fa "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *msg" "size_t msglen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen"
.Fa "int ph"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sig" "size_t siglen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fn nqssize "nqsalg alg" "nqssz *sz"
.Ft const char *
.Fn nqsname "nqsalg alg"
.Ft int
.Fn nqsfind "const char *name" "nqsalg *alg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions make keys, sign and verify with the module-lattice
signature ML-DSA (FIPS 204) and the stateless hash-based signature SLH-DSA
(FIPS 205).
Keys and signatures are byte strings in the encodings the standards
define.
.Ss Algorithms
.Vt nqsalg
names the parameter set:
.Bl -column "NQSLHK128S" "SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128s" "pk" "sk" "signature" -offset indent
.It Sy constant Ta Sy name Ta Sy pk Ta Sy sk Ta Sy signature
.It Dv NQMLDSA44 Ta ML-DSA-44 Ta 1312 Ta 2560 Ta 2420
.It Dv NQMLDSA65 Ta ML-DSA-65 Ta 1952 Ta 4032 Ta 3309
.It Dv NQMLDSA87 Ta ML-DSA-87 Ta 2592 Ta 4896 Ta 4627
.It Dv NQSLH128S Ta SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s Ta 32 Ta 64 Ta 7856
.It Dv NQSLH128F Ta SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f Ta 32 Ta 64 Ta 17088
.It Dv NQSLH192S Ta SLH-DSA-SHA2-192s Ta 48 Ta 96 Ta 16224
.It Dv NQSLH192F Ta SLH-DSA-SHA2-192f Ta 48 Ta 96 Ta 35664
.It Dv NQSLH256S Ta SLH-DSA-SHA2-256s Ta 64 Ta 128 Ta 29792
.It Dv NQSLH256F Ta SLH-DSA-SHA2-256f Ta 64 Ta 128 Ta 49856
.It Dv NQSLHK128S Ta SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128s Ta 32 Ta 64 Ta 7856
.It Dv NQSLHK128F Ta SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128f Ta 32 Ta 64 Ta 17088
.It Dv NQSLHK192S Ta SLH-DSA-SHAKE-192s Ta 48 Ta 96 Ta 16224
.It Dv NQSLHK192F Ta SLH-DSA-SHAKE-192f Ta 48 Ta 96 Ta 35664
.It Dv NQSLHK256S Ta SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256s Ta 64 Ta 128 Ta 29792
.It Dv NQSLHK256F Ta SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256f Ta 64 Ta 128 Ta 49856
.El
.Pp
Sizes are in bytes.
The
.Ql s
sets give small signatures and slow signing, the
.Ql f
sets fast signing and larger signatures.
.Pp
.Fn nqssize
stores the sizes of
.Fa alg
in
.Fa *sz ,
a
.Vt nqssz
with the members
.Va pk ,
.Va sk
and
.Va sig .
.Fn nqsname
returns the name of
.Fa alg
as in the table, or
.Dv NULL
for a value that is not an
.Vt nqsalg .
.Fn nqsfind
is its inverse: it stores in
.Fa *alg
the algorithm whose name is exactly
.Fa name
(case matters).
.Ss Keys
.Fn nqskg
makes a key pair from the operating system's random source
.Pq Xr nqrand 3 ,
writing the public key to
.Fa pk
and the secret key to
.Fa sk .
.Fn nqskgd
makes it from the standard's seed instead: the 32-byte xi for ML-DSA, or
SK.seed || SK.prf || PK.seed (3n bytes: 48, 72 or 96) for SLH-DSA.
It exists for test vectors and for keys that must be derived again; the
seed is as secret as the key.
The seed may overlap
.Fa pk
or
.Fa sk ,
and on any error both are cleared.
.Ss Signing and verifying
.Fn nqsign
signs the
.Fa msglen
bytes at
.Fa msg
with the secret key
.Fa sk
of
.Fa sklen
bytes and writes the signature to
.Fa sig ,
a buffer of
.Fa siglen
bytes; the signature's length is stored in
.Fa *outlen
when
.Fa outlen
is not
.Dv NULL .
Signing is hedged: fresh randomness is mixed in, so signatures of one
message differ.
.Pp
.Fa ctx
is the FIPS 204/205 context string,
.Fa ctxlen
bytes, at most 255;
.Dv NULL
and 0 give the empty context.
A signature verifies only under the context it was made with, which keeps
signatures made for one purpose from being accepted for another.
.Pp
.Fa ph
selects the interface: 0 for pure ML-DSA or SLH-DSA, or an
.Vt nqhalg
.Pq Xr nqhash 3
for HashML-DSA or HashSLH-DSA, where
.Fa msg
is still the message and is hashed by the function.
Any of the twelve hashes may be used; for SHAKE128 and SHAKE256 the digest
is 32 and 64 bytes.
.Pp
.Fn nqsignd
is
.Fn nqsign
with the standard's per-signature randomness
.Fa rnd
given by the caller: exactly 32 bytes for ML-DSA, n bytes (16, 24 or 32)
for SLH-DSA.
All zero bytes give the deterministic variant of the standard.
.Pp
.Fn nqvrfy
checks that
.Fa sig
of
.Fa siglen
bytes is a signature of
.Fa msg
under the public key
.Fa pk
with the context
.Fa ctx
and the interface
.Fa ph
used to sign.
.Ss Buffers
Output buffers may be larger than the algorithm's size; only the defined
number of bytes is written.
Input keys and signatures must have exactly the algorithm's size.
The signature buffer may overlap the message (signing in place).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Every function except
.Fn nqsname
returns
.Dv NQOK
(0) on success or a negative error code:
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Bq Er NQEARG
.Fa alg
is not an
.Vt nqsalg ;
a pointer is
.Dv NULL
with a nonzero length, or an output pointer is
.Dv NULL ;
.Fa ctxlen
exceeds 255;
.Fa ph
is neither 0 nor an
.Vt nqhalg ;
or, for
.Fn nqskgd
and
.Fn nqsignd ,
.Fa seed
or
.Fa rnd
is
.Dv NULL
or not the standard's length.
.Fn nqsfind
returns it for a
.Dv NULL
argument.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa pklen ,
.Fa sklen
or
.Fa siglen
is smaller than the algorithm's size.
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
A key or signature given as input does not have the algorithm's length or
encoding.
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
.Fn nqvrfy :
the signature does not verify.
A verification never returns
.Dv NQOK
unless the signature is valid.
.It Bq Er NQERNG
.Fn nqskg
or
.Fn nqsign :
the operating system's random source failed.
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
.Fn nqsfind :
no algorithm has that name.
.El
.Pp
On any failure,
.Fn nqsign
and
.Fn nqsignd
set
.Fa *outlen
to 0, and when signing itself fails they wipe the signature buffer.
.Fn nqsname
returns
.Dv NULL
for an unknown algorithm.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Make a key pair, sign and verify (the program
.Pa docs/examples/sign.c
of the source tree):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <noqtis.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
  static uint8_t pk[1952], sk[4032], sig[3309];
  const uint8_t msg[] = "results v1";
  size_t n = 0;
  int rc = nqskg(NQMLDSA65, pk, sizeof pk, sk, sizeof sk);
  if (rc == NQOK)
    rc = nqsign(NQMLDSA65, sk, sizeof sk, msg, sizeof msg - 1, NULL, 0, 0,
                sig, sizeof sig, &n);
  nqwipe(sk, sizeof sk);
  if (rc == NQOK)
    rc = nqvrfy(NQMLDSA65, pk, sizeof pk, msg, sizeof msg - 1, NULL, 0, 0,
                sig, n);
  printf("%s\en", nqerr(rc));
  return rc == NQOK ? 0 : 1;
}
.Ed
.Pp
Sizes at run time, for code that takes the algorithm as a parameter:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nqsalg alg;
nqssz sz;
if (nqsfind("SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128s", &alg) == NQOK &&
    nqssize(alg, &sz) == NQOK)
  printf("%s: %zu-byte signatures\en", nqsname(alg), sz.sig);
.Ed
.Pp
Build with
.Ql cc prog.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs noqtis) .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-sign 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-verify 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqerr 3 ,
.Xr nqhash 3 ,
.Xr nqwipe 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T FIPS 204: Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard
.%Q NIST
.%D August 2024
.Re
.Rs
.%T FIPS 205: Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Standard
.%Q NIST
.%D August 2024
.Re
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Key generation and signing run in constant time with respect to the secret
key, seed and randomness; ML-DSA signing is also first-order masked (two
shares).
Wipe secret keys with
.Xr nqwipe 3
when done.
Outside test vectors, prefer
.Fn nqsign
to
.Fn nqsignd :
the hedged variant keeps fault and side-channel attacks that rely on
repeated signatures harder.
